This useEffect is calling the parent callback `onSubmit()` to communicate state changes. Parent-child communication should not use useEffect. Instead, this logic should be lifted to the parent component so it can directly watch `reimbursementAccount?.isSuccess` and handle the navigation.

**Suggested fix:**
Move this success-handling logic to the parent component that owns the navigation flow:

```tsx
// In parent component
const [reimbursementAccount] = useOnyx(ONYXKEYS.REIMBURSEMENT_ACCOUNT);

useEffect(() => {
    if (reimbursementAccount?.isSuccess && !isDocusignStepRequired) {
        clearReimbursementAccountFinishCorpayBankAccountOnboarding();
        Navigation.setNavigationActionToMicrotaskQueue(() => {
            navigateToNextStep();
        });
    }
}, [reimbursementAccount?.isSuccess]);

// Pass down simple callbacks
<Agreements onBackButtonPress={...} onSubmit={navigateToNextStep} />
```

This follows React's unidirectional data flow, eliminates synchronization issues, and makes the data flow clearer.

